**Read:** [Metal Recycling: Opportunities, Limits, Infrastructure — UNEP International Resource Panel](../sources/Metal-Recycling-UNEP-IRP.lingua#r_40JXFY43ST442BB8MJEAYJT9N1), the entire full report and original references for the selected case; [Tópicos sobre a Reciclagem de Metais e Sustentabilidade — Ronaldo Luiz Corrêa dos Santos](../sources/Reciclagem-de-Metais-e-Sustentabilidade-CETEM.lingua#r_7X28NJBWY8Z5Y1BVZXHVC4MHSX), the complete monograph; [Non-ferrous Metals Industries — European Commission BREF](../sources/Nonferrous-Metals-Industries-BREF.lingua#r_19ZD7KKDWVWM20MXVNCQZJMCDB), whole relevant secondary-production/refining and residual chapters; [Extractive Metallurgy of Copper — Schlesinger, Sole, Davenport, and Alvear Flores](../sources/Extractive-Metallurgy-of-Copper.lingua#r_47NCQVYD4J2DXH9AV48XDMNHJ7), all recycling chapters as an additional complete case, when available.

End-of-use products and manufacturing scrap are designed mixtures with joined materials, coatings, phases, geometry, and uncertain history. Collection, separation, preparation, chemistry, refining, alloy adjustment, and specification determine what is actually recovered for use. A collection rate, recycled input fraction, process recovery, and accepted product yield measure different things.

Use the whole UNEP report and complete metal/process cases to follow the actual element network. Thermodynamic distribution, mechanical separation, contamination, dilution, energy, economics, equipment, and human work constrain routes. More processing can improve one recovery while losing another constituent or shifting burdens to reagents, residuals, or utilities.

Distinguish reuse, remelting into a compatible grade, refining into another product, use in a lower-specification application, and residual treatment. A nominally closed loop does not prove indefinitely stable impurity populations or eliminate primary feed and maintenance needs. Preserve actual quantities, quality, time, uncertainty, and system boundaries.

**Work:** read the entire UNEP report and Portuguese CETEM monograph, then reconstruct a complete complex-product or multimetal recovery case. Independently close several consequential elements from collection through qualified products and residuals. Compare two separation/refining or product-design alternatives under changed feed and impurity assumptions. Explain the physical, informational, infrastructural, and working capabilities required to sustain the better-supported route.

**Continue:** [Preserve material identity and quality evidence through transfers, processing, and use](Material-identity-custody-traceability-and-changing-product-state.lingua#r_61D4D2RMGDTB681KWP8058BKR1).

